## 1. Two keys, one future

Reflection about $1/2$ gives $f(1-x)=f(x)$. Explore the merged paths interactively and then generate a static comparison plot.

{{interactive_demo:0}}

{{visualization:0}}

<details><summary>Reveal the exact argument</summary>

Expanding gives $4(1-x)(1-(1-x))=4(1-x)x=4x(1-x)$. Determinism then preserves equality under every later update. Thus every nonempty orbit suffix generated by $x$ is identical to the suffix generated by $1-x$.

</details>

