{{demo:1}}

{{visualization:1}}

<details><summary>Reveal the inverse-tree proof</summary>

For $a=\sqrt{1-y}$, substituting $(1-a)/2$ gives $(1-a)(1+a)=1-a^2=y$. Reflection supplies the upper branch. Composing one valid inverse at each level constructs a valid ancestor at the requested depth.

</details>

