## 3. The angle behind the chaos

Writing $x=\sin^2	heta$ turns one update into angle doubling: $f(\sin^2	heta)=\sin^2(2	heta)$. Consequently $f^n(\sin^2	heta)=\sin^2(2^n	heta)$. This identity explains exponential separation and exact structure at once.

<details><summary>Reveal the trigonometric derivation</summary>

Use $1-\sin^2	heta=\cos^2	heta$ and $\sin(2	heta)=2\sin	heta\cos	heta$, then induct on the number of updates.

</details>

## 4. Finite precision means eventual repetition, not long period

A deterministic machine with $N$ states repeats among its first $N+1$ visited states. The statement is an upper bound; short cycles remain possible.

