{{visualization:2}}

<details><summary>Reveal the finite-state theorem</summary>

The $N+1$ listed states occupy only $N$ possible values, so two coincide by the pigeonhole principle. Once a state repeats, all later states repeat with the same offset. No lower bound on the cycle length follows.

</details>

