## Takeaway

Equivalent keys, explicit inverse branches, a closed angular formula, exceptional absorbing states, and short rounding-dependent cycles all survive regardless of how random a selected sample appears. Statistical diagnostics remain useful, but cryptographic security requires an adversarial analysis of the complete, precisely specified generator.
